[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Thread Management in React Native: JS Thread, UI Thread, Shadow Thread, and Background Tasks"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"React Native relies on a multi-threaded architecture to ensure smooth user experiences while executing complex business logic. Understanding how threads interact is crucial for building high-performance cross-platform applications."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"The Core Threads in React Native"},{"order":4,"type":"bullet_point","text":"JS Thread: Executes all JavaScript code, including application logic, API calls, state management (Redux, Zustand), and the React reconciliation algorithm."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"UI (Main) Thread: Responsible for rendering native UI components, handling user touch gestures, and drawing frames on the screen (maintaining 60/120 FPS)."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Shadow Thread (Layout Thread): Computes the layout of views using Yoga (Flexbox) before sending the final coordinates to the UI Thread."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"Handling Heavy Computations in JavaScript"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"Because the JS Thread is single-threaded, running heavy calculations directly on it will block user interactions and cause dropped frames (jank). To prevent this, offload intensive tasks using modern React Native modules or background execution libraries."},{"order":9,"type":"code","text":"import { InteractionManager } from 'react-native';

const runHeavyTaskAfterInteractions = () => {
  InteractionManager.runAfterInteractions(() => {
    // Perform non-urgent heavy computations here
    console.log("Executing heavy task after animations/gestures complete");
  });
};"},{"order":10,"type":"subheading","text":"Background Tasks and Native Modules"},{"order":11,"type":"paragraph","text":"For operations that must run independently of the React lifecycle (such as syncing data or playing audio), developers utilize native background tasks or libraries like react-native-background-actions."},{"order":12,"type":"code","text":"import backgroundTask from 'react-native-background-actions';

const sleep = (time) => new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, time));

const veryIntensiveTask = async (taskDataArguments) => {
  const { delay } = taskDataArguments;
  await new Promise(async (resolve) => {
    for (let i = 0; backgroundTask.isRunning(); i++) {
      console.log("Running background sync...");
      await sleep(delay);
    }
  });
};

const options = {
  taskName: 'Sync',
  taskTitle: 'Syncing Data',
  taskDesc: 'Running background synchronization',
  taskIcon: { name: 'ic_launcher', type: 'mipmap' },
  color: '#ff00ff',
  parameters: { delay: 5000 },
};

// Start background task
// await backgroundTask.start(veryIntensiveTask, options);"},{"order":13,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"Effective thread management in React Native means keeping the UI Thread free for rendering and gestures, letting the Shadow Thread calculate layouts asynchronously, and delegating long-running operations away from the JS Thread."}]
